' A file named after a library, lying beside the script, is read in place of
' the library, and everything the library defines is then simply absent. The
' importer now says so on stderr; what this test pins down is the resolution
' itself - the neighbour wins, in both backends.
IMPORT CLI

DIM bad = 0.0

IF CLI.SHADOW_MARK$() <> "local" THEN
    bad = bad + 1
    PRINT "IMPORT CLI did not read the file beside the script"
ENDIF

IF bad = 0 THEN PRINT "RESULTS: 1 passed, 0 failed" ELSE PRINT "RESULTS: 0 passed, 1 failed"
